---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Projects - NandLabs" description="Projects I'm working on: Memorii, VirtualEmployee, and Yapper.">
  <header class="page-header shell"><h1>Projects</h1></header>
  <section class="section shell project-pair" aria-label="NandLabs projects">
    <article class="project-card project-card-text" id="memorii">
      <div>
        <h2>Memorii</h2>
        <p>A memory system for agents. It tracks ontology, execution state, and a solver graph.</p>
        <p><a href="/writing/memorii">Read about Memorii</a> / <a href="https://github.com/nrag/Memorii">GitHub</a></p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="project-card project-card-text" id="virtualemployee">
      <div>
        <h2>VirtualEmployee</h2>
        <p>This is an idea I'm working on: a virtual employee that works inside a Slack workspace. The implementation is still in its early days. I'm hoping to have a preview by the end of 2026.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="project-card" id="yapper">
      <img src="/images/yapper.png" width="96" height="96" alt="Yapper app icon" />
      <div>
        <h2>Yapper</h2>
        <p>Yapper was an experiment I attempted in 2012: an encrypted messaging app with a calendar, polls, and a shared task list. I recognized the need for an extensibility platform but never built it.</p>
        <p>I built it for Windows Phone but never ported it to iOS or Android. Many of the ideas were correct, but not building for those platforms hurt. In hindsight, it should have been an enterprise product.</p>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/nrag/yapper">GitHub</a></p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
